		<p>You may place cups or small beverage cans in the cup holders.</p>
		<note type="warning" id="e02200">
			<p>Hot Liquids</p>
			<p>Do not place uncovered cups with hot liquid in the cup holders while the vehicle is in motion. If the hot liquid spills, you could be burned. A driver who is burned could lose control of the vehicle.</p>
		</note>
		<note type="warning" id="e02201">
			<p>Keep cans or bottles out of direct sunlight, and do not put them in a hot vehicle. They could explode.</p>
		</note>
		<note type="note" id="e02202">
			<ul id="e02203">
				<li>
					<p>To prevent spillage, keep your drinks sealed while driving. If liquid spills, it may get into the vehicle’s electrical or electronic system and damage parts.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>When cleaning spilled liquids, do not use heat to dry the cup holders. This may damage the cup holders.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
	</conbody>
